// # Alias Dictionary
// ==================
//
// Multi-word dictionary values that a study token must select as ONE word.
// Same role and same mechanism as cases/2Dvortex/system/aliasDict: the study
// harness substitutes a single token value, and OpenFOAM's `$name` expansion
// (which searches enclosing dictionary scopes) turns it back into the
// multi-word scheme text inside a sub-dictionary.

// ## Level-set time scheme, selected by the PSI_DDT study token.
//
// WHY THIS AXIS EXISTS (2026-08-19). The coupled droplet runs `default Euler`
// in ddtSchemes, and that default reaches fvm::ddt(psi) in alphaEqn.H -- so the
// LEVEL SET, not just momentum, is integrated first order in time here, while
// every kinematic ladder (2Dvortex, 3Dshear, 3Ddeformation) runs
// CrankNicolson 1. The kinematic-vs-coupled comparison therefore differed in
// TWO things, not one, and this token controls the second.
//
// The mechanism that makes it worth a study rather than a footnote: with the
// simpleLinearImplicit source the per-step factor is 1/(1 - a*dt). For a strain
// `a` that alternates sign with zero mean -- which is what a standing mode-4
// parasitic current produces -- one +/- pair gives 1/(1 - z^2) > 1 with
// z = a*dt, so implicit Euler RECTIFIES a zero-mean oscillating strain into
// one-sided growth of |psi| at O(z^2) per pair. The Crank-Nicolson factor
// (1 + z/2)/(1 - z/2) is the (1,1) Pade approximant and is symmetric: the pair
// product is exactly 1 and the leading rectification is O(z^3).
//
// PREDICTION to falsify: the 4x dt refinement already measured moved the drain
// half-life 0.046-0.049 -> 0.052-0.060 (+~20%), which is what the same O(z^2)
// term predicts at z ~ 0.023. CrankNicolson attacks the SAME term, so it should
// buy ~20% and no more. Much more => the rectification model is incomplete.
// Worse => the competing effect wins: CrankNicolson is only A-stable, with
// amplification -> -1 at grid scale, so it never damps the mode-4 noise that
// L-stable Euler does damp.
//
// MOMENTUM STAYS ON Euler regardless: raising the momentum time order at the
// calibrated capillary step is MEASURED to diverge on this problem (N=64,
// dt=2e-5: backward peaks ~48, CrankNicolson 0.9 ~1e+102 -- see the ddtSchemes
// comment in fvSchemes). Only ddt(psi) is switched.

// BackwardDdt (BDF2) is the DISCRIMINATING third point, added 2026-08-19 after
// the CrankNicolson arm failed. The three schemes separate ORDER from DAMPING:
//
//   scheme          order   A-stable   L-stable   rectification of an
//                                                 oscillating zero-mean strain
//   Euler             1        yes       YES      O(z^2), one-sided
//   CrankNicolson     2        yes       no       O(z^3)
//   backward (BDF2)   2        yes       YES      O(z^3)
//
// CrankNicolson removed the O(z^2) rectification and made the coupled droplet
// WORSE at N >= 64 (diverged at t = 0.046 / 0.030 against Euler's 0.058 /
// 0.040), which says the L-stable damping it gave up was worth more than the
// rectification it removed -- its amplification factor tends to -1 as z -> -inf,
// so it never damps the grid-scale mode-4 capillary noise that Euler does.
//
// backward is the scheme that has BOTH properties: second order in time AND
// L-stable (stiffly accurate, amplification -> 0 as z -> -inf). So it decides
// between the two readings of the CrankNicolson failure:
//   * if the failure was LOSS OF DAMPING, backward should behave like Euler or
//     better, and the ~20% rectification gain should finally show up;
//   * if the failure was SECOND ORDER ITSELF -- e.g. the wider stencil
//     resolving and propagating the mode-4 perturbation that Euler's numerical
//     dissipation smears -- backward should fail like CrankNicolson.
//
// Neither outcome is expected to be a FIX: the mechanism study established that
// the drain is seeded entirely by curvature error (with the exact-curvature
// force, relative volume error is 0.000e+00 at every N for both Euler and CN,
// with the source ON). This arm is mechanism, not remedy.
//
// MOMENTUM STAYS ON Euler here as in every other arm. That is not a detail:
// `backward` on MOMENTUM is measured to diverge on this capillary problem at
// the calibrated step (N=64, dt=2e-5: peak ~48), and is stable only at
// dt_sigma/8. Only ddt(psi) is switched.
EulerDdt          Euler;
CrankNicolsonDdt  CrankNicolson 1;
BackwardDdt       backward;

